// EXPECT: [E100]
// EXPECT-TEXT: `i in data` as an index test was retired: `in` means membership in a set, and data's indices are the range `0..data.len`. Write `i in 0..data.len` (or `i < data.len`).
// I.78 (DECIDE-X): `i in a` read as `i < a.len`, while every other language reads it as "i is one
// of a's elements". Both meanings compile, so the old one could not simply change: it is refused,
// naming the replacement, and only once nothing uses it does `x in a` become element membership
// (I.79).
func first_or_zero(data u8[], i usize) u8 {
    if i in data {
        return data[i]
    }
    return 0
}
func main() i32 {
    return 0
}
